Your issue lies in the form action URL for your reset password view. The form should point to `/reset-password` instead of `/reset-password/{token}` since you're submitting the token, email, and password before navigating to the confirmation page. Ensure your `auth/reset-password.blade.php` form looks like this:

```html
<form method="POST" action="{{ route('password.update') }}">
    @csrf

    <!-- Your existing form fields -->

    <button type="submit">Reset Password</button>
</form>
```

This will correctly submit the form to the `/reset-password` route, where your validation and password reset logic is defined. Make sure you have the correct route name `password.update` in your routes file:

```php
Route::post('/reset-password', function (Request $request) {
    // Your existing code...
})->middleware('guest')->name('password.update');
```

With these adjustments, clicking "Reset Password" should now correctly redirect to the login page after a successful password reset.

