The error occurs because `BrowserAnimationsModule` internally imports `BrowserModule`, which re-exports `CommonModule`. In your standalone component, you should import `CommonModule` instead of `BrowserAnimationsModule` to access common directives like `NgIf` and `NgFor`.

Since you are in a standalone project without any module, you need to explicitly import `CommonModule`:

```typescript
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-component',
  template: '<div *ngIf="condition">Hello World</div>'
})
export class MyComponent {
  condition = true;
}
```

Additionally, if you need animations, import `NoopAnimationsModule` (or `BrowserAnimationsModule` for immediate animations) in your standalone component or module:

```typescript
import { NoopAnimationsModule } from '@angular/platform-browser/animations';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-component',
  template: '<div [@myAnimation]="condition">Hello World</div>',
  animations: [
    trigger('myAnimation', [transition('* => *', animate(500))])
  ]
})
export class MyComponent {
  condition = true;
}
```

This approach avoids re-importing `BrowserModule` and resolves the errors.

