To detect changes in the required validator of a parent control within a ControlValueAccessor implementation, you can listen for changes in the `NgControl.control` object. Specifically, you need to subscribe to the `statusChanges` observable provided by Angular's reactive forms API. This will notify you whenever the status (including validators) of the form control changes.

Here’s how you can implement this:

```typescript
import { NgControl } from '@angular/forms';

constructor(private ngControl: NgControl) {}

ngOnInit(): void {
  const control = this.ngControl.control;

  if (control) {
    // Subscribe to statusChanges to detect validator changes
    control.statusChanges.subscribe(() => {
      this.parentRequires = control.hasValidator(Validators.required);
    });

    // Initial check
    this.parentRequires = control?.hasValidator(Validators.required) ?? false;
  }
}
```

This approach ensures that you are notified whenever the required validator (or any other validators) is added or removed from the form control, allowing you to dynamically update your UI based on these changes.

