To ensure `VistaFacturasComponent` calls `filterFacturas()` whenever `searchBarService.searchTextSignal` updates, you can use RxJS's `toObservable` utility to create an observable from the signal and subscribe to it in your component. Here’s how:

1. Import necessary utilities:
   ```typescript
   import { Component } from '@angular/core';
   import { toObservable } from '@angular/core/rxjs-interop';
   ```

2. Modify `VistaFacturasComponent` to use the observable:
   ```typescript
   constructor(private facturaService: FacturaService, public searchBarService: SearchBarService) {
     // Convert searchTextSignal to an Observable and subscribe to it.
     const searchText$ = toObservable(this.searchBarService.searchTextSignal);

     searchText$.subscribe(text => {
       this.filterFacturas();
     });
   }

   filterFacturas(): void {
     let text = this.searchBarService.searchTextSignal();

     if (!text) 
       this.filteredFacturasArray.set(this.facturasArray);

     this.filteredFacturasArray.set(
       this.facturasArray.filter(factura => factura?.numero.toString().includes(text))
     );
   }
   ```

This approach ensures that `filterFacturas()` is called every time the search text changes, updating the filtered list accordingly.

