To achieve dynamic loading of child components and transfer data from them to the parent component, you can use `ViewContainerRef` as shown in your attempt. However, for transferring data back to the parent, consider using an `Output` decorator with an event emitter in the child component. Here’s how:

1. **Child Component (`client-registration-form.component.ts`):**
   ```typescript
   import { Component, Output, EventEmitter } from '@angular/core';
   import { ClientRegistrationModel } from '../models/client-registration.model';

   @Component({
     selector: 'app-client-registration-form',
     template: `
       <input [(ngModel)]="clientRegistrationMoel.firstName" placeholder="First Name">
       <!-- other form fields -->
       <button (click)="onSubmit()">Submit</button>
     `
   })
   export class ClientRegistrationFormComponent {
     @Output() onFormSubmit = new EventEmitter<ClientRegistrationModel>();

     clientRegistrationMoel: ClientRegistrationModel = new ClientRegistrationModel("", "", "", "");

     onSubmit() {
       this.onFormSubmit.emit(this.clientRegistrationMoel);
     }
   }
   ```

2. **Parent Component (`landing-home.component.ts`):**
   ```typescript
   import { Component, ViewChild, ViewContainerRef } from '@angular/core';
   import { ClientRegistrationFormComponent } from '../client-registration-form/client-registration-form.component';

   @Component({
     selector: 'app-landing-home',
     template: `
       <ng-container #container></ng-container>
     `
   })
   export class LandingHomeComponent {
     @ViewChild('container', { read: ViewContainerRef }) container!: ViewContainerRef;

     ngAfterViewInit() {
       this.container.createComponent(ClientRegistrationFormComponent);
     }

     handleFormSubmit(formModel: ClientRegistrationModel) {
       console.log('Form submitted with data:', formModel);
       // Handle the form submission here
     }
   }
   ```

3. **Parent Component Template (`landing-home.component.html`):**
   ```html
   <ng-container #container></ng-container>
   ```

By using `Output` and an event emitter, you can easily pass data from the child component to the parent when needed. This approach avoids the need for multiple `*ngIf` conditions and keeps your code clean and maintainable.

