The error occurs because `item` in your template is being treated as a string by Angular's template type checker, even though you've defined it as `MenuItem | undefined`. This mismatch can happen if the `trackBy` function or other parts of the template are not correctly handling the item type.

To fix this issue, ensure that the `trackBy` function in your template uses the correct property to uniquely identify each menu item. In your case, use `item.id`:

```typescript
@Component({
  standalone: true,
  imports: [NxWelcomeComponent, RouterModule, MenuItemComponent],
  selector: 'angular-monorepo-root',
  templateUrl: './app.component.html',
  styleUrl: './app.component.scss',
