To address the issue of displaying a loading status during lazy-loaded route transitions, you can implement a global loading indicator. This involves creating a service that tracks whether any lazy-loaded modules are currently being loaded and updating your UI accordingly.

1. **Create a Loading Service**:
   ```typescript
   // src/app/loading.service.ts
   import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
   import { BehaviorSubject } from 'rxjs';

   @Injectable({
     providedIn: 'root'
   })
   export class LoadingService {
     private loadingSubject = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(false);
     readonly isLoading$ = this.loadingSubject.asObservable();

     startLoading() {
       this.loadingSubject.next(true);
     }

     stopLoading() {
       this.loadingSubject.next(false);
     }
   }
   ```

2. **Update `app.routes.ts`**:
   ```typescript
   // src/app/app-routing.module.ts
   import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
   import { RouterModule, Routes } from '@angular/router';
   import { LoadingService } from './loading.service';

   const routes: Routes = [
     {
       path: '',
       redirectTo: '/dashboard',
       pathMatch: 'full'
     },
     {
       path: 'login',
       component: LoginComponent,
       title: 'Login',
     },
     {
       path: '',
       canActivateChild: [AuthGuard],
       loadChildren: () => import(`./app-authorized.routes`).then((r) => r.appAuthorizedRoutes),
       resolve: { isLoading: LoadingService.isLoading$ }
     },
     { path: '**', redirectTo: '/dashboard' }
   ];

   @NgModule({
     imports: [RouterModule.forRoot(routes)],
     exports: [RouterModule]
   })
   export class AppRoutingModule {}
   ```

3. **Update `app.component.html`**:
   ```html
   <!-- src/app/app.component.html -->
   <div *ngIf="loadingService.isLoading$ | async" class="loader">Loading...</div>
   <!-- Your existing content here -->
   ```

4. **Inject and Use the Service in Authorized Routes**:
   Ensure that `AuthGuard` or any resolver uses the service to start/stop loading.

By implementing this approach, you can display a loading indicator while lazy-loaded modules are being loaded, improving the user experience during transitions.

