To store and process each row's radio button selection in Livewire 3, you need to bind the radio buttons to your component's properties and handle the form submission correctly. Here’s how:

1. **Bind Radio Buttons**: Use Livewire's `wire:model` directive to bind the radio buttons to your component's properties.

2. **Handle Form Submission**: In your `Save()` method, loop through the selected values and create records accordingly.

Here is a simplified version of your code:

```blade
<!-- Form Page -->
<form wire:submit.prevent="save">
    @foreach ($UserDetail as $key => $UserDetails)
        <div>
            {{ $key + 1 }}
            {{ $UserDetails->id }}
            {{ $UserDetails->name }}
            <input type="radio" name="attendance[{{ $UserDetails->id }}]" value="yes" wire:model="TableInput.{{ $UserDetails->id }}"> Yes
            <input type="radio" name="attendance[{{ $UserDetails->id }}]" value="no" wire:model="TableInput.{{ $UserDetails->id }}"> No
        </div>
    @endforeach

    <button type="submit">SAVE</button>
</form>
```

```php
// Controller
class StudentAttendance extends Component
{
    public $name;
    public $id;
    public $TableInput = [];

    public function mount()
    {
        $this->UserDetail = User::all();
    }

    public function save()
    {
        foreach ($this->TableInput as $userId => $attendance) {
            Data::create([
                'user_id' => $userId,
                'status' => $attendance
            ]);
        }
    }
}
```

This setup ensures that each row's radio button selection is stored in `TableInput` and processed during form submission.

