To achieve your goal of extracting just the grouped dates from the `groupBy` result in Laravel, you can use the `keys()` method on the collection returned by `groupby`. This will give you an array of the keys (dates) without the nested collections. Here's how you can modify your code:

```php
$this->StudentList = Student::get();
$data = $this->StudentList->sortBy('date', SORT_NATURAL)->groupBy('date');

// Extracting only the grouped dates as a flat array
$groupedDates = $data->keys()->all();

dd($groupedDates);
```

This code first sorts your `StudentList` by date and groups them. Then, it uses the `keys()` method to get an array of keys (dates) from the grouped collection, and finally calls `all()` to convert the collection to a plain PHP array. This will give you the desired output:

```php
array:14 [▼ 
 "2024-01-01" 
 "2024-01-02" 
 "2024-01-03" 
 "2024-01-04" 
 "2024-01-05" 
]
```

