To display items from index 1 of an array of strings in Angular, you can use the `@for` block with a tracking expression and leverage the `$index` variable to skip the first item:

```angular-html
<ul>
  @for (item of arr; track item) {
    <li *ngIf="$index > 0">{{ item }}</li>
  }
</ul>
```

This code uses `*ngIf` with `$index > 0` to exclude the first item. The tracking expression `track item` ensures that each item is uniquely identified, which is necessary for proper rendering and performance.

Alternatively, you can slice the array in your component's TypeScript file:

```typescript
@Component({
  template: `
    <ul>
      @for (item of arr.slice(1); track item) {
        <li>{{ item }}</li>
      }
    </ul>
  `,
})
export class AppComponent {
  arr = [ "str1", "str2", "str3", "str4", "str5" ];
}
```

This approach avoids the need for `$index` and directly skips the first element in the template.

