The issue likely stems from how Angular's change detection works with `OnPush` components and signals. When you update `typeSignal`, Angular marks your component for check but doesn't automatically trigger a re-evaluation of the `charts` signal unless it is explicitly marked or its dependencies are updated.

To ensure that `charts` updates correctly, consider marking the `charts` signal for check when `typeSignal` changes:

```typescript
import { computed } from '@angular/core';

this.typeSignal.set(newType); // Update typeSignal

// Manually mark charts for check to trigger re-evaluation
this.charts = computed(() => {
  // ... existing logic ...
});
```

Alternatively, if you're using a reactive form or another mechanism that updates `typeSignal`, ensure it triggers change detection. You can also use Angular's `ChangeDetectorRef` to manually detect changes:

```typescript
import { ChangeDetectorRef } from '@angular/core';

constructor(private cdr: ChangeDetectorRef) {}

this.typeSignal.set(newType);
this.cdr.detectChanges(); // Manually trigger change detection
```

This ensures that the `charts` signal is re-evaluated and your template updates accordingly.

