The issue arises because your `CategoryComponent` does not properly handle the dynamic form array structure. Specifically, the `FormArray` elements are unnamed and should be accessed using their index within the parent component's template. Here’s how you can resolve it:

1. Ensure that each child component receives its correct index.
2. Use the `*ngFor` directive correctly in your parent component to pass the form group and index.

Here is a revised version of your code:

**Parent Component:**
```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app',
  template: `
    <form [formGroup]="categoryForm">
      <div *ngFor="let category of categories.controls; let i = index" [formGroupName]="i">
        <app-category 
          [categories]="categories"
          [formGroup]="category"
          [index]="i"></app-category>
      </div>
      <!-- Add and Remove Category buttons -->
    </form>
  `,
  standalone: true,
  imports: [ReactiveFormsModule, JsonPipe, NgFor, CategoryComponent],
})
export class AppComponent {
  categoryForm!: FormGroup;
  categories = this.fb.array([]);

  constructor(private fb: FormBuilder) {}

  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.categoryForm = this.fb.group({
      categories: this.categories
    });
  }

  // ... other methods ...
}
```

**Child Component:**
```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-category',
  template: `
    <label>
      Category ID:
      <input type="text" formControlName="categoryID">
    </label>
    <label>
      Category Name:
      <input type="text" formControlName="categoryName">
    </label>
    <button (click)="removeCategory()">Remove</button>
  `,
  standalone: true,
  imports: [ReactiveFormsModule, NgFor]
})
export class CategoryComponent {
  @Input() categories!: FormArray;
  @Input() formGroup!: FormGroup;
  @Input() index!: number;

  removeCategory() {
    this.categories.removeAt(this.index);
  }
}
```

This setup ensures that each `FormGroup` in the `FormArray` is correctly bound and can be manipulated by the child component.

