The `x-nav-link` component in Laravel Breeze does not have additional built-in attributes beyond `href` and `active`. However, you can conditionally render links based on user roles or other conditions using Livewire's event listeners or by leveraging Blade templating within the `navigation.blade.php` file.

To conditionally show a nav link for admin users only, you could use a combination of Blade directives. For example:

```blade
@auth
    @if(auth()->user()->isAdmin())
        <x-nav-link href="{{ route('admin.dashboard') }}">
            {{ __('Admin Dashboard') }}
        </x-nav-link>
    @endif
@endauth
```

This code checks if the user is authenticated and then further checks if they are an admin before rendering the link. This approach allows you to conditionally display navigation links based on user roles or other conditions without needing additional attributes on `x-nav-link`.

