In Laravel 11, adding a service provider does not require manual modification of `config/app.php`. Instead, you should use the `ServiceProvider::addProviderToBootstrapFile` method to automatically add your service provider to the application's bootstrapping process. Here’s how you can do it:

```php
use Illuminate\Support\ServiceProvider;

class PackageServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function register(): void
    {
        // Register services here if needed.
    }

    public function boot(): void
    {
        // Boot logic here.
    }
}

// In your package's service provider file, add:
use App\Providers\PackageServiceProvider; // Adjust the namespace as necessary

ServiceProvider::addProviderToBootstrapFile(PackageServiceProvider::class);
```

This method ensures that your service provider is automatically registered in `bootstrap/providers.php`, improving maintainability and reducing the risk of configuration errors.

