The error occurs because `toSignal` converts an observable into a read-only signal, not a writable one. To fix this issue, you need to directly use `signal` for the writable part of your application where you want to update values. Here's how you can adjust your code:

```typescript
import { Component, effect, signal } from '@angular/core';
import { AppService } from "../app.service";

@Component({
  selector: 'app-parent',
  templateUrl: './parent.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./parent.component.css']
})
export class ParentComponent {

  translations = signal({ data: [] }); // Use `signal` for writable part

  constructor(private appService: AppService) {
    this.translations.set(this.appService.getTranslations().value); // Initialize with observable value
    effect(() => {
      console.log('translation API:', this.translations());
    });
  }

  changeValue(): void {
    this.translations.update(value => ({ ...value, data: { hello: 'hallo' } }));
  }
}
```

In this solution:
- `translations` is a writable signal initialized with the value from the observable.
