To detect changes in the required validator of a control, you can listen to the `statusChanges` event of the form control. This event emits whenever the status (validity) of the control changes, including when validators are added or removed.

Here's how you can implement it:

```typescript
import { NgControl } from '@angular/forms';

constructor(private ngControl: NgControl) {}

ngOnInit(): void {
  this.ngControl.control?.statusChanges.subscribe(() => {
    this.parentRequires = this.ngControl.control?.hasValidator(Validators.required) ?? false;
  });
}
```

This approach ensures that you are notified whenever the required validator is toggled on or off, allowing you to update your UI accordingly.

