To include specific Angular services for use with lazy-loaded standalone components, you can leverage the `providedIn` token in your service decorator and set it to `'root'`. However, since you're using standalone components, a better approach is to create a shared module that provides these services. This way, when you load this module via `loadChildren`, the services are also provided.

Here's how you can do it:

1. Create a new feature module for your services:
   ```shell
   ng generate module auth-services --module app.module
   ```

2. Move your login-related services into this new module and provide them there:
   ```typescript
   // src/app/auth-services/auth-services.module.ts
   import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
   import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';
   import { AuthGuardService, AuthService } from './auth.services';

   @NgModule({
     imports: [CommonModule],
     providers: [
       AuthGuardService,
       AuthService
     ]
   })
   export class AuthServicesModule {}
   ```

3. Update your `app-routing.module.ts` to include this module:
   ```typescript
   // src/app/app-routing.module.ts
   const routes: Routes = [
     { path: '', redirectTo: '/login', pathMatch: 'full' },
     {
       path: 'login',
       component: LoginComponent,
       title: 'Login'
     },
     {
       path: '',
       canActivateChild: [AuthGuard],
       loadChildren: () => import(`./app-authorized.routes`).then((r) => r.appAuthorizedRoutes),
     },
     { path: '**', redirectTo: '/login' }
   ];
   ```

4. In `app-authorized.routes.ts`, load the new module:
   ```typescript
   // src/app/app-authorized.routes.ts
   export const appAuthorizedRoutes: Routes = [
     {
       path: 'dashboard',
       component: DashboardComponent,
       canActivate: [AuthGuard],
       title: 'Dashboard'
     },
     {
       path: 'settings',
       component: SettingsComponent,
       canActivate: [AuthGuard],
       title: 'Settings'
     }
   ];
   ```

This setup ensures that the services are only loaded when the authorized routes are accessed, improving initial load times.

