In Angular 17 with standalone components, you can't provide services in the root as you did before. Instead, use `providedIn: 'any'` to share a service across all eagerly loaded modules and instances within lazy-loaded modules. For your loader service:

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { NgxUiLoaderService } from 'ngx-ui-loader';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'any',
})
export class LoaderService {
  constructor(private ngxLoader: NgxUiLoaderService) {}

  startLoader() {
    this.ngxLoader.start();
  }

  stopLoader() {
    this.ngxLoader.stop();
  }
}
```

Ensure `LoaderService` is imported and used in your components:

```typescript
import { Component, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { LoaderService } from './services/loader.service';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  standalone: true,
  template: `<div>App</div>`
})
export class AppComponent {
  constructor(private loaderService: LoaderService) {}

  ngOnInit() {
    this.loaderService.startLoader();
    // Your logic here
    this.loaderService.stopLoader();
  }
}
```

This setup ensures the service works correctly in both eagerly and lazily loaded modules.

