To display items from index 1 of an array of strings in Angular 17 using the `@for` loop, you can filter the array to exclude the first element before rendering. Here's how:

```angular-ts
@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: `
    @for (item of arr.slice(1); track item) {
      {{ item }}
    }
  `,
})
export class AppComponent {
  arr = ["str1", "str2", "str3", "str4", "str5"];
}
```

In this example, `arr.slice(1)` creates a new array starting from the second element (index 1). The `@for` loop then iterates over these elements, displaying each one. This approach leverages the `slice` method to skip the first item and use the `@for` loop for rendering the rest.

