To ensure both main and thumbs Swipers initialize correctly across route changes in Angular with SSR, you can encapsulate their initialization logic within a single function that runs outside of the Angular zone. This approach prevents redundant initializations and ensures smooth operation during routing transitions.

Here's how to structure your `ngAfterViewInit` method:

```typescript
import { NgZone } from '@angular/core';

// ...

ngAfterViewInit() {
  this.zone.runOutsideAngular(() => {
    const swiperParams = {
      // main Swiper parameters
    };

    const swiperParams1 = {
      spaceBetween: 10,
      // thumbs Swiper parameters
    };

    Object.assign(this.swiper2.nativeElement, swiperParams1);
    this.swiper1.nativeElement.initialize();

    Object.assign(this.swiper2.nativeElement, swiperParams);
    this.swiper2.nativeElement.initialize();
  });
}
```

This setup ensures both Swipers are initialized only once when the component is first loaded or reloaded after a route change. Adjust `swiperParams` and `swiperParams1` to fit your specific configuration needs.

