In Laravel 11, adding a service provider does not require manual modification of `config/app.php`. Instead, you should use the `ServiceProvider::addProviderToBootstrapFile` method to automatically add your service provider to the application's bootstrapping process. Here’s how you can do it:

```php
use Illuminate\Support\ServiceProvider;

class PaytmWalletServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function register(): void
    {
        // Register any services or bindings here.
    }

    public function boot(): void
    {
        // Boot logic goes here.
    }
}

// In your package, add the following line to automatically include it:
use Illuminate\Support\ServiceProvider;

ServiceProvider::addProviderToBootstrapFile(PaytmWalletServiceProvider::class);
```

This method ensures that your service provider is included in the `bootstrap/providers.php` file without needing to manually edit `config/app.php`. This approach simplifies package development and keeps configuration clean.

