It sounds like you have multiple CSS files influencing the same part of your application, causing issues with dropdowns or other elements on your admin home page. To address this in Laravel 10 using Livewire and Jetstream, you can define a custom CSS file for your specific component to ensure it has unique styles.

First, create a `css` method in your Livewire component to return the path of your custom CSS file:

```php
class AdminHome extends Component
{
    // ...

    protected function css()
    {
        return __DIR__.'/../../resources/css/admin-home.css';
    }
}
```

This ensures that only this component loads its specific styles, avoiding conflicts with other components or global styles.

If you need to further customize the dropdown specifically, ensure your `admin-home.css` includes unique selectors for your dropdown:

```css
/* resources/css/admin-home.css */
.dropdown-menu {
    /* Your custom styles here */
}
```

By defining a `css` method in your Livewire component and using specific CSS rules, you can isolate and manage the styles affecting your admin home page without interfering with other parts of your application.

