In Laravel 11, middleware are managed differently compared to previous versions. Since you're using Spatie's Permission package and encountered an error indicating that the target class does not exist, you need to ensure the necessary middleware classes from this package are registered correctly.

Although there is no `app/Http/Kernel.php` file in Laravel 11 by default, you can still register custom middleware. You should add the Spatie permission middleware to your application's `bootstrap/app.php` file within the `$middleware` array:

```php
$app->withMiddleware(function (Middleware $middleware) {
    // Registering Spatie Permission Middleware
    $middleware->web(append: [
        \Spatie\Permission\Middlewares\RoleMiddleware::class,
        \Spatie\Permission\Middlewares\PermissionMiddleware::class,
        \Spatie\Permission\Middlewares\RoleOrPermissionMiddleware::class,
    ]);
});
```

This approach ensures that the required middleware from Spatie's Permission package is included in your application, resolving the "Target class [permission] does not exist" error.

