The error occurs because `toSignal` returns an instance of `Signal`, not `WritableSignal`. To convert an observable to a writable signal, you need to use `toObservable` first and then convert the resulting signal to a writable one using `signal`.

Here's how you can modify your code:

1. Use `toObservable` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop` to create an observable from your service.
2. Convert this observable-wrapped signal to a writable signal.

```typescript
import { Component, effect, signal, WritableSignal } from '@angular/core';
import { AppService } from "../app.service";
import { toObservable, toSignal } from "@angular/core/rxjs-interop";

@Component({
 selector: 'app-parent',
 templateUrl: './parent.component.html',
 styleUrls: ['./parent.component.css']
})
export class ParentComponent {

 translations: WritableSignal = signal({ data: [] });

 constructor(private appService: AppService) {
   const obsTranslations = toObservable(this.appService.getTranslations());
   this.translations = toSignal(obsTranslations, { initialValue: { data: [] } });
   effect(() => {
     console.log('translation API:', this.translations());
   });
 }

 changeValue(): void {
   this.translations.set({ data: { hello: 'hallo' } })
 }
}
```

This approach ensures that `translations` is a writable signal, allowing you to use `.set()` to update its value.

