In Angular 16 with signals, change detection might not trigger automatically outside of the Angular zone, even after calling `signal.update()`. This is because signals rely on Angular's change detection mechanism to reflect updates in the view. To ensure changes are detected, you need to re-enter the Angular zone.

Modify your `click` method to use `NgZone.run()`:

```typescript
import { NgZone } from '@angular/core';

// ...

click(): void {
  this.zone.run(() => {
    this.title.update((value) => value + "!!");
  });
}
```

By wrapping the update call in `zone.run()`, you ensure that Angular processes the change and triggers a change detection run, updating the view accordingly.

