The error occurs because Angular's template type checker infers `item` in your `AppComponent`'s template as a `string`, not as `MenuItem | undefined`. This mismatch causes the type check to fail, even though you've defined `item` as `MenuItem | undefined` in `MenuItemComponent`.

To resolve this issue, ensure that the type of `item` in the template matches its actual type. Since `item` is an input from `MenuItemComponent`, it should be typed correctly there.

In your `app.component.html`, change:

```html
@for (item of menu; track item.id) {
```

To:

```html
@for (item of menu; track item.id) {
  <menu-item [item]="item"></menu-item>
}
```

This explicitly binds each `MenuItem` to the `item` input in `MenuItemComponent`, ensuring that Angular correctly infers its type as `MenuItem`.

Additionally, update your `MenuItemComponent`'s @Input decorator:

```typescript
@Input({ required: true }) item: MenuItem | undefined = undefined;
```

