To extract only the grouped dates from your `groupBy` result in Laravel, you can iterate over the collection and collect the keys (dates) into an array. Here's how you can do it:

```php
$groupedDates = array_keys($data->all());
```

This code uses `array_keys()` to get all the keys (dates) from the grouped data. Since `$data` is a collection, calling `all()` converts it to an array first.

Your final code would look like this:

```php
$this->StudentList = Student::get();
$data = $this->StudentList->sortBy('date', SORT_NATURAL)->groupBy('date');

$groupedDates = array_keys($data->all());
```

This will give you the desired output as an array of dates without any nested collections.

