To use an index in `@for` in Angular 17, you can explicitly define it using the `let` keyword as shown below:

```angular-html
@for (user of users; track user.id; let i = $index) {
  {{ user.name + i }}
}
```

Note that `$index` is used instead of `index`. This syntax correctly defines an index variable within the `@for` loop. The `track` keyword helps Angular optimize performance by maintaining a relationship between your data and DOM nodes.

Here, `i` will hold the index value for each iteration, allowing you to use it in your template expressions as needed.

