In Laravel 11, you no longer manually add service providers in `config/app.php`. Instead, use the `ServiceProvider::addProviderToBootstrapFile` method to automatically register your provider. Here’s how:

```php
use Illuminate\Support\ServiceProvider;

// Inside your package's ServiceProvider class or a custom one:
ServiceProvider::addProviderToBootstrapFile(Anand\LaravelPaytmWallet\PaytmWalletServiceProvider::class);
```

This line should be placed in the `boot` method of your service provider. This approach ensures that your provider is registered when the application boots, without needing to modify `config/app.php`.

For example:

```php
namespace Anand\LaravelPaytmWallet;

use Illuminate\Support\ServiceProvider;

class PaytmWalletServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function boot(): void
    {
        // Use this method to register your service provider.
        ServiceProvider::addProviderToBootstrapFile(self::class);
    }

    public function register(): void
    {
        // Register bindings or other setup logic here.
    }
}
```

This change simplifies the process and keeps configuration files cleaner.

