To remove the `browser` folder when using `ng build --watch` with a custom output path, you can set the `outputPath.browser` to an empty string in your `angular.json`. However, since you want to avoid modifying the `angular.json`, you can use the following command:

```shell
ng build --base-href=/x/ --output-path=/projects/project-x-backend/wwwroot \
--watch --configuration development --verbose --extra-webpack-config='{ "output": { "path": "/projects/project-x-backend/wwwroot" } }'
```

This command sets a custom output path without creating the `browser` subfolder. Note that you might need to adjust your webpack configuration if additional settings are required for your deployment.

Alternatively, ensure your `angular.json` is configured as follows:

```json
{
  "projects": {
    "project-x": {
      "architect": {
        "build": {
          "options": {
            "outputPath": {
              "base": "/projects/project-x-backend/wwwroot",
              "browser": ""
            }
          },
          // other options...
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This configuration allows you to use `ng build --watch` with a custom output path without the `browser` subfolder.

