```php
use AsAction;
use AsCommand;

class SitemapGenerateAction
{
    public string $commandSignature = 'sitemap:generate';
    public string $commandDescription = 'Generate the sitemap';

    protected array $sitemapData;

    public function handle(): void
    {
        // Handle logic here.
    }

    public function asCommand(Command $command): void
    {
        // Command logic here.
    }
}
```

Next, add your action class to the `commands` array in your `config/tinker.php` file:

```php
'commands' => [
    \App\Actions\SitemapGenerateAction::class,
],
```

This configuration allows you to run your custom command via Tinker. Note that while `Console/Kernel.php` is not required for registering commands, the `asCommand` method in your action class should properly define how the command behaves when invoked from Tinker or other CLI interfaces.

