In Angular 16, you can load a standalone component as a dialog without using routing or preloading by directly creating an instance of the component and adding it to your application's DOM. Since the component is standalone, you don't need to import it into any module.

Here’s how you can do it:

1. Ensure your standalone component is defined with `standalone: true` in its metadata.
2. Use Angular's `ComponentFactoryResolver` to dynamically load and instantiate the component.

Example code snippet:
```typescript
import { ComponentFactoryResolver, ComponentRef, NgModuleRef } from '@angular/core';
import { YourStandaloneComponent } from './your-standalone.component';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: `<button (click)="openDialog()">Open Dialog</button>`
})
export class AppComponent {
  constructor(private componentFactoryResolver: ComponentFactoryResolver) {}

  openDialog() {
    const factory = this.componentFactoryResolver.resolveComponentFactory(YourStandaloneComponent);
    const componentRef: ComponentRef<YourStandaloneComponent> = factory.create();
    // Optionally, you can attach the component to a specific host element
    document.body.appendChild(componentRef.location.nativeElement);
    // If needed, get the NgModuleRef for further manipulation
    const ngModuleRef: NgModuleRef<YourStandaloneComponent> = componentRef.encapsulation;
  }
}
```

This approach allows you to dynamically load and display your standalone component as a dialog without involving routing or preloading.

