The error you're encountering occurs because `createLoanPaymentsForm.controls` returns an object with keys as control names, not an array that can be iterated over directly. To correctly loop through a `FormArray`, you should use the `controls` property of the `FormArray`.

Here's how to fix it:

1. Ensure your `FormGroup` is set up properly:
   ```typescript
   createLoanPaymentsForm: FormGroup = this.formBuilder.group({
     payments: this.formBuilder.array([]),
   });
   ```

2. In your template, use the `controls` property of the `FormArray` to iterate over it:

```html
<form [formGroup]="createLoanPaymentsForm">
  <div formArrayName="payments" *ngFor="let payment of createLoanPaymentsForm.get('payments').controls; let i = index">
    <label>Payment {{i+1}}</label>
    <input type="text" formControlName="amount">
    <!-- Add more fields as needed -->
  </div>
  <button (click)="addPayment()">Add</button>
  <button *ngIf="createLoanPaymentsForm.get('payments').length > 0" (click)="removeLastPayment()">Remove Last</button>
</form>
```

3. Implement methods to add and remove payments:

```typescript
addPayment() {
  const control = this.formBuilder.control('');
  (<FormArray>this.createLoanPaymentsForm.get('payments')).push(control);
}

removeLastPayment() {
  if (this.createLoanPaymentsForm.get('payments').length > 0) {
    this.createLoanPaymentsForm.get('payments').removeAt(this.createLoanPaymentsForm.get('payments').length - 1);
  }
}
```

This setup allows you to dynamically add, remove, and edit payments in your form.

