In Angular 17 with standalone components, you can't provide services in the root module as you would in older versions. For your `LoaderService` to work across multiple components, you need to provide it at a higher level than individual components but not at the root level. One approach is to use a shared module that provides the service and then import this shared module wherever needed.

Here’s how you can do it:

1. Create a shared module:
```typescript
// shared.module.ts
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';
import { LoaderService } from './services/loader.service';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [],
  imports: [CommonModule],
  providers: [LoaderService]
})
export class SharedModule {}
```

2. Import the `SharedModule` in your main module or any other module where you need the service:
```typescript
// app.module.ts
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { AppComponent } from './app.component';
import { SharedModule } from './shared/shared.module';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [AppComponent],
  imports: [BrowserModule, SharedModule],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule {}
```

3. Use the `LoaderService` in your components:
```typescript
// app.component.ts
import { Component, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { LoaderService } from './services/loader.service';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  templateUrl: './app.component.html'
})
export class AppComponent {
  constructor(private loaderService: LoaderService) {}

  ngOnInit() {
    this.loaderService.startLoader();
    // Your logic here
    this.loaderService.stopLoader();
  }
}
```

This setup ensures that `LoaderService` is available across your application, similar to how you would provide it in the root module in older Angular versions.

