To display items from index 1 of an array in Angular's `@for` loop, you can use the `slice` method to exclude the first element. Here’s how:

```typescript
@Component({
  template: `
    @for (item of arr.slice(1); track item) {
      {{ item }}
    }
  `,
})
export class AppComponent {
  arr = ["str1", "str2", "str3", "str4", "str5"];
}
```

In this example, `arr.slice(1)` creates a new array starting from the second element (index 1). The `track item` ensures Angular tracks each item uniquely for efficient rendering and updates.

