The issue likely stems from how Angular's change detection works with signals and computed values. When you update `typeSignal`, the `charts` signal should ideally recompute, but if it doesn't, consider adding an effect to manually trigger updates:

```typescript
import {effect} from '@angular/core';

// Inside your component class
effect(() => {
  console.log('Charts recomputed');
  // This ensures that charts is recomputed whenever typeSignal changes.
}, [typeSignal]);
```

This effect will run every time `typeSignal` changes, ensuring the `charts` signal updates and triggers a re-render in your template.

Additionally, ensure your component is set to `OnPush` change detection strategy:

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-your-component',
  templateUrl: './your-component.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./your-component.component.css'],
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
})
export class YourComponent {
  // ... existing code ...
}
```

This setup ensures Angular only checks for changes when inputs or signals change, which should help in your scenario.

