To address the bugged dropdown issue in Laravel 10 Jetstream/Livewire, you need to ensure that your CSS styles are correctly scoped and not conflicting with each other. Given that the white theme on the home page works fine but causes issues elsewhere, it suggests a specific CSS file or style might be affecting multiple parts of your application.

You can instruct Pulse to load additional stylesheets for your Livewire component by defining a `css` method in your component:

```php
class YourComponent extends Component
{
    protected function css()
    {
        return __DIR__.'/../../path/to/your-specific-styles.css';
    }
}
```

This ensures that the specific CSS file only affects this component, avoiding conflicts with other styles. Make sure to replace `../../path/to/your-specific-styles.css` with the actual path to your CSS file.

Additionally, if you are using Tailwind CSS, consider creating a dedicated configuration for your component to avoid loading unnecessary classes:

```js
export default {
    content: [
        './resources/views/livewire/your-component.blade.php',
    ],
};
```

Place this configuration in the appropriate directory and reference it in your CSS entrypoint. This helps isolate styles and prevents conflicts.

By isolating the problematic styles, you can identify and fix the issue affecting the dropdown menu without disrupting other parts of your application.

