The error "localStorage is not defined" occurs because `localStorage` is a browser API and isn't available in non-browser environments like server-side rendering or unit tests. To resolve this issue, you should provide a fallback mechanism that works across different execution contexts.

You can achieve this by using the `providedIn: 'root'` strategy to ensure your service is a singleton and then conditionally use `localStorage`. Here’s how:

1. Ensure your `AuthService` is provided at the root level:
   ```typescript
   import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

   @Injectable({
     providedIn: 'root',
   })
   export class AuthService {
     // ... existing code ...
   }
   ```

2. Modify your service to conditionally use `localStorage` based on the environment:

   ```typescript
   import { Injectable, Inject, PLATFORM_ID } from '@angular/core';
   import { isPlatformBrowser } from '@angular/common';

   @Injectable({
     providedIn: 'root',
   })
   export class AuthService {
     public isAuth = new BehaviorSubject(false);

     constructor(
       private router: Router,
       @Inject(PLATFORM_ID) private platformId: Object
     ) {}

     autoSignIn() {
       if (isPlatformBrowser(this.platformId)) {
         const email = localStorage.getItem('email');
         if (email) {
           this.isAuth.next(true);
           this.router.navigate(['/dashboard']);
         }
       } else {
         // Fallback logic for non-browser environments
         console.warn('Running in a non-browser environment. No local storage available.');
       }
     }

     signIn(email: string) {
       if (isPlatformBrowser(this.platformId)) {
         localStorage.setItem('email', email);
         this.isAuth.next(true);
         this.router.navigate(['/dashboard']);
       } else {
         // Fallback logic for non-browser environments
         console.warn('Running in a non-browser environment. No local storage available.');
       }
     }

     signOut() {
       if (isPlatformBrowser(this.platformId)) {
         localStorage.removeItem('email');
         this.isAuth.next(false);
         this.router.navigate(['/auth']);
       } else {
         // Fallback logic for non-browser environments
         console.warn('Running in a non-browser environment. No local storage available.');
       }
     }
   }
   ```

This approach ensures your service works correctly both in browser and non-browser environments by checking if the platform is a browser before using `localStorage`.

