The issue arises because your checkboxes are likely bound to an array in Vue but you're using `ref` for handling selections. To fix this, ensure each checkbox updates its corresponding item in the `selectedButtons` array individually. Here’s how you can adjust your code:

1. **Update Checkbox Binding:**
   Bind each checkbox directly to a specific index in the `selectedButtons` array.

```vue
<div v-for="(button, index) in buttons" :key="index">
  <input type="checkbox" @change="toggleButtonSelection(index)" :value="button.buttonTitle" v-model="selectedButtons[index].buttonTitle">
  {{ button.buttonTitle }}
</div>
```

2. **Define `toggleButtonSelection` Method:**
   Create a method to handle checkbox changes.

```vue
<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue';
import { useForm } from '@inertiajs/vue3';

const selectedButtons = ref([]); // Initialize as an array of objects

function toggleButtonSelection(index) {
  if (selectedButtons.value[index]) {
    delete selectedButtons.value[index];
  } else {
    selectedButtons.value[index] = true;
  }
}
</script>
```

3. **Update Form Submission:**
   Ensure the `buttons` field in your form submission is correctly set.

```javascript
const submit = () => form.post('/message', {
  data: { buttons: Object.values(selectedButtons).filter(Boolean) },
});
```

This approach ensures that only selected checkboxes are sent to the server, preventing all from being checked when any single checkbox changes.

