1. Ensure you have imported `FormsModule` from `@angular/forms`.

2. Add `FormsModule` to the `imports` array of the NgModule that contains your `TaskComponent`. Typically, this would be done in your main `AppModule`, or a specific feature module if `TaskComponent` is part of a larger feature.

Here’s an example:

```typescript
// app.module.ts (or task.module.ts)
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { FormsModule } from '@angular/forms';

@NgModule({
  imports: [
    FormsModule, // Add this line to import FormsModule
    // other imports...
  ],
  declarations: [TaskComponent], // Ensure TaskComponent is declared here
  // other configurations...
})
export class AppModule { }
```

After adding `FormsModule`, the `ngModel` directive should work correctly in your template:

```html
<!-- task.component.html -->
<label for="framework">
  Favorite Framework:
  <input id="framework" type="text" [(ngModel)]="favoriteFramework" />
</label>
```

If you are using a feature module, make sure to declare `TaskComponent` and import `FormsModule` in that module. If the error persists, restart your development server to ensure all changes take effect.

For more details, refer to the documentation excerpt about [What should I import?](https://angular.io/guide/ngmodule#what-should-i-import).

