To achieve your goal of using multiple repositories with different database connections in Laravel 10, you need to ensure that each repository instance has its own connection and isn't shared among instances. Here’s how you can adjust your code:

1. **Ensure Each Repository Instance Has Its Own Connection**:
   - In `RepositoryServiceProvider`, register a new instance of the repository for each connection name.

```php
class RepositoryServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function register(): void
    {
        $this->app->bind(UserRepositoryInterface::class, fn () => new UserRepository(User::connection('db01')));
        $this->app->bind(fn () => new UserRepository(User::connection('db02')), 'user_repo02');
        $this->app->bind(fn () => new UserRepository(User::connection('db03')), 'user_repo03');
    }
}
```

