To detect changes in the required validator dynamically, you can subscribe to the `valueChanges` event of the form control and check for the presence of the `required` validator each time the value changes. This approach ensures that your component reacts to any changes in validation requirements.

Here’s how you can implement this:

```typescript
import { NgControl } from '@angular/forms';

constructor(private #control: NgControl) {}

ngOnInit(): void {
  this.#control.valueAccessor = this;

  // Subscribe to valueChanges to detect when the control's value or validators change.
  this.#control.control?.valueChanges.subscribe(() => {
    const parentRequires = this.#control.control?.hasValidator(Validators.required);
    this.parentRequires = parentRequires ?? false;
  });
}
```

This code snippet subscribes to `valueChanges`, which will be triggered whenever the control's value or validators change, allowing you to update `parentRequires` accordingly.

