Yes, you can load a standalone component in Angular 16 as a dialog without using routing or preloading. Since your component is standalone and doesn't rely on an `NgModule`, you can directly instantiate it and open it as a dialog. Here’s how:

First, ensure your standalone component is correctly defined with the `standalone: true` metadata.

```typescript
// my-standalone-dialog.component.ts
@Component({
  standalone: true,
  selector: 'my-standalone-dialog',
  template: `
    <div>
      This is a standalone dialog!
    </div>
  `,
})
