The issue arises because Angular's template compiler expects `item` in your `AppComponent`'s `*ngFor` directive to be of type `MenuItem`, but you are not explicitly defining the type for `item`. When using `track item.id`, TypeScript infers that `item` is a string, which causes the error.

To resolve this, ensure that the type of `item` matches your `MenuItem` interface. You can do this by adding the type annotation directly in the template:

```typescript
@for (let item of menu; track item.id) {
  {{(item as MenuItem).name}} 
}
```

Alternatively, you can define a local variable with the correct type to avoid the issue:

```typescript
<ul>
  @for (const item of menu; track item.id) {
    <li>{{(item as MenuItem).name}}</li>
  }
</ul>
```

This ensures that `item` is correctly typed as `MenuItem`, resolving the TypeScript error.

