The `[disabled]` binding will update automatically when `isSubmitting` changes due to the manual change detection call.

For consistency and readability, consider moving the `ChangeDetectorRef` injection and usage into a method:

```typescript
export class LoginComponent {
  isSubmitting = false;

  constructor(private ref: ChangeDetectorRef) {}

  onLogin() {
    this.isSubmitting = true;
    // Assuming auth.login returns an Observable
    this.auth.login(this.username.value, this.password.value, this.rememberMe.value)
      .pipe(filter(authenticated => authenticated))
      .subscribe({
        next: () => {
          this.isSubmitting = false; 
          this.ref.markForCheck();
        }
      });
  }
}
```

This keeps your component logic clean and ensures that change detection is properly triggered.

