To address the issue of displaying a loading status during lazy-loaded route transitions in your Angular application, you can implement a global loading indicator. This involves creating a service to manage the loading state and updating the UI accordingly.

1. **Create a Loading Service**:
   ```typescript
   import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
   import { BehaviorSubject } from 'rxjs';

   @Injectable({
     providedIn: 'root'
   })
   export class LoaderService {
     private isLoadingSubject = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(false);
     isLoading$ = this.isLoadingSubject.asObservable();

     startLoading() {
       this.isLoadingSubject.next(true);
     }

     stopLoading() {
       this.isLoadingSubject.next(false);
     }
   }
   ```

2. **Update `app.routes.ts`**:
   ```typescript
   import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
   import { RouterModule, Routes } from '@angular/router';
   import { LoaderService } from './loader.service';

   const routes: Routes = [
     // ... other routes
     {
       path: '',
       canActivateChild: [AuthGuard],
       loadChildren: () => import(`./app-authorized.routes`).then((r) => r.appAuthorizedRoutes),
       resolve: {
         isLoading: (route, state, routeConfig, loaderService: LoaderService) => {
           loaderService.startLoading();
           return routeConfig.loadChildren().then(() => loaderService.stopLoading());
         }
       }
     },
     // ... other routes
   ];

   @NgModule({
     imports: [RouterModule.forRoot(routes)],
     exports: [RouterModule],
     providers: [LoaderService]
   })
   export class AppRoutingModule {}
   ```

3. **Update the Navigation Bar Component**:
   ```typescript
   import { Component, OnInit } from '@angular/core';
   import { LoaderService } from '../loader.service';

   @Component({
     selector: 'app-navigation-bar',
     template: `
       <div *ngIf="!isLoading$ | async" class="navigation-bar">
         <!-- Navigation bar content -->
       </div>
       <div *ngIf="isLoading$ | async" class="loading-indicator">
         Loading...
       </div>
     `,
   })
   export class NavigationBarComponent implements OnInit {
     constructor(private loaderService: LoaderService) {}

     ngOnInit() {}
   }
   ```

This setup ensures that the navigation bar is hidden while the lazy-loaded modules are being loaded, providing a better user experience.

