The issue you're encountering is due to Jetstream's default behavior of redirecting unauthenticated users to the dashboard. To resolve this without changing the redirection logic, ensure your API routes are correctly defined and not inadvertently triggering web middleware.

In your `api.php`, make sure no web middleware groups are applied:

```php
Route::group(['namespace' => '\App\Http\Controllers\Api', 'middleware' => ['auth:sanctum', config('jetstream.auth_session'), 'verified']], function() {
    // Your API routes here...
});
```

Additionally, ensure your `navigation-menu.blade.php` uses the correct route for API endpoints. For example:

```blade
<a href="{{ route('assets.index') }}" @if (request()->routeIs('dashboard')) class="d-none" @endif>
    {{ __('Assets') }}
</a>
```

This ensures that when on the dashboard, the "Assets" link is hidden (`class="d-none"`).

If you still face issues, check your `config/auth.php` to ensure the correct guards are configured for API authentication. Also, verify there's no global redirection logic in your application that might be causing unexpected behavior.

By ensuring only `sanctum` middleware is applied and correctly defining routes, you should avoid unwanted redirections to the dashboard when accessing API endpoints.

