To migrate your Angular templates to the new syntax introduced in Angular 17 efficiently, you can use the `@angular/core` schematic provided by Angular. Run the following command:

```shell
ng generate @angular/core:control-flow
```

This will automatically convert your existing `*ngIf` and `*ngFor` directives to the new `@if` and `@for` syntax.

For example, your old template:
```html
<div *ngIf="!dynamicWidth">
  <!-- content -->
</div>

<ul>
  <li *ngFor="let item of count | numberRange; trackBy: trackItem; let i = $index">
    {{ item }}
  </li>
</ul>
```

Would be migrated to:
```html
@if (!dynamicWidth) {
  <!-- content -->
}

@for (item of count | numberRange; track item; let i = $index) {
  {{ item }}
}
```

This approach ensures your templates are updated efficiently and maintain the new syntax standards.

