The issue arises because you're trying to access an array as if it were an integer in your Blade template. Specifically, this line:

```blade
@foreach($row['status'] as $r)
```

Here, `$row['status']` might not be an array but an integer value, leading to the error "Trying to access array offset on value of type int."

To resolve this, ensure that `$row['status']` is indeed an array. You can add a check before accessing it:

```blade
@foreach($row['status'] as $r)
    Status- {{ $r['groupName'] }}
@endforeach
```

Should be preceded by verifying the data type:

```blade
@if(is_array($row['status']))
    @foreach($row['status'] as $r)
        Status- {{ $r['groupName'] }}
    @endforeach
@endif
```

This ensures that you only attempt to loop through `$row['status']` if it is an array, preventing the error.

