In Laravel 11, you should add your service provider in the `bootstrap/providers.php` file instead of `config/app.php`. Here’s how to do it:

1. Ensure your service provider class is correctly defined and placed in the `app/Providers` directory.
2. Open or create the `bootstrap/providers.php` file.

Add your service provider class to the `$providers` array, like this:

```php
<?php

return [
    // Other providers...
    Anand\LaravelPaytmWallet\PaytmWalletServiceProvider::class,
];
```

This will automatically register your service provider when Laravel boots up. If you have manually created the provider and not using Artisan commands to generate it, ensure it’s added here.

For automatic registration via `composer.json`, include:

```json
"extra": {
    "laravel": {
        "providers": [
            "Anand\\LaravelPaytmWallet\\PaytmWalletServiceProvider"
        ]
    }
}
```

After updating your `composer.json`, run `composer dump-autoload` to apply changes.

