To create loading indicators for iframes within an `@for` loop in Angular 17, you can use the `@defer` directive along with a `@loading` block to manage lazy-loading content gracefully. Here’s how you can achieve this:

```angular-html
@for (link of youtubeLinks; track $index) {
  @defer {
    <iframe [src]="link" sandbox="allow-scripts"></iframe>
  } @loading {
    <div>Loading...</div> <!-- Display a loading indicator -->
  }
}
```

In the above code, each iframe is wrapped in an `@defer` block. When Angular encounters this directive, it will initially display the content of the `@loading` block (in this case, "Loading..."). Once the iframe's source has been fetched and loaded, the actual iframe content replaces the loading indicator.

This approach ensures that your page loads more quickly by deferring the loading of iframes until they are needed, improving Core Web Vitals such as LCP.

