This template uses `@if` to check if the `movies` array exists. If it does, it further checks its length. Based on this condition, it renders either the recent movie details or a default message when no movies are available.

Ensure that your component class has an initialized `movies` array to avoid type-related issues. This approach avoids using logical OR (`||`) and leverages Angular's template syntax effectively.

