The issue you're facing with checkboxes selecting all options might be due to how Vue handles form data and checkbox states. Ensure that each checkbox has a unique `v-model` binding to the correct state in your Vue component. Here’s an example of how you can handle this:

1. **Ensure Unique State for Each Checkbox:**
   ```vue
   <template>
     <div v-for="button in buttons" :key="button.id">
       <input type="checkbox" 
              :id="`button-${button.id}`"
              :value="button.buttonTitle"
              v-model="selectedButtons[button.id]"
              @change="form.validate(`buttons.${button.id}`)">
       <label :for="`button-${button.id}`">{{ button.buttonTitle }}</label>
     </div>
   </template>

   <script setup>
   import { useForm } from '@inertiajs/vue3';

   const form = useForm({
     title: null,
     body: null,
     buttons: {}, // Initialize as an object
     images: [],
     date: null,
     time: null,
   });

   const submit = () => {
     form.post('/message', { preserveScroll: true, onSuccess: () => form.reset() });
   };
   </script>
   ```

2. **Update Form Submission Logic:**
   Ensure your `submit` function correctly handles the form submission with Inertia.

3. **Controller and Validation:**
   Your controller should handle the JSON-encoded buttons array properly:
   ```php
   public function message(Request $request)
   {
       $validated = $request->validate([
           'title' => 'required',
           'body' => 'required',
           'buttons' => 'nullable|array',
           // other validations...
       ]);

       if ($request->hasFile('sentimages')) {
           $validated['images'] = Storage::disk('public')->put('sentimages', $request->file('sentimages'));
       }

       message::create($validated);
       return redirect()->route('CMS')->with('successfully added');
   }
   ```

This setup ensures that each checkbox is bound to a unique state in Vue, preventing the issue of all checkboxes being selected when one is clicked.

