To detect changes in the required validator of the parent control, you can listen for changes in the `NgControl.control` object. Specifically, you need to subscribe to the `statusChanges` observable provided by Angular's reactive forms API. This will notify you whenever the status (including validators) of the form control changes.

Here’s how you can implement it:

```typescript
import { NgControl } from '@angular/forms';

constructor(private ngControl: NgControl) {}

ngOnInit(): void {
  this.ngControl.control?.statusChanges.subscribe(() => {
    this.parentRequires = this.ngControl.control?.hasValidator(Validators.required) ?? false;
    // Update your UI or perform other actions based on the new status
  });
}
```

This approach ensures that you are notified whenever the required validator (or any other validators) changes, allowing you to dynamically update your component's state accordingly.

