In Angular 16, `entryComponents` should be added in the `declarations` array of your root module (`AppModule`) instead of the `entryComponents` array. This ensures that these components are recognized and can be used as dialog or modal components throughout your application.

Here's how you can update your `app.module.ts`:

```typescript
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    // Other components...
    PayResultDialogComponent,
    MessageBoxComponent
  ],
  imports: [
    BrowserModule,
    // Other modules...
  ],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule { }
```

By adding `PayResultDialogComponent` and `MessageBoxComponent` to the `declarations` array, these components are now available for use in your application. Note that if you need to use them as entry components specifically for lazy-loaded modules, you should add them there as well.

