In Laravel, you can specify the controller class using either `use` statement or `->namespace()` method in your route definition. Both approaches are correct but serve slightly different purposes and contexts.

To directly use the fully qualified class name:
```php
use App\Http\Controllers\Admin\PhotoController;

Route::prefix('admin')->middleware('auth')->group(function () {
    Route::resource('photos', PhotoController::class);
});
```

Or, to group routes under a specific namespace without explicitly using `use` in each route definition:
```php
Route::prefix('admin')->namespace('App\Http\Controllers\Admin')->middleware('auth')->group(function () {
    Route::resource('photos', PhotoController::class);
});
```

