To achieve your goal of extracting just the grouped dates from the `groupBy` result in Laravel Livewire, you can use the `keys()` method on the collection returned by `groupby`. This will give you an array containing only the keys (dates) from the grouped data. Here's how you can modify your code:

```php
$this->StudentList = Student::get();
$data = $this->StudentList->sortBy('date', SORT_NATURAL)->groupBy('date');

// Extracting just the dates as a flat array
$groupedDates = $data->keys()->all();

// Outputting the grouped dates
dd($groupedDates);
```

This code first sorts and groups your `Student` records by date. Then, it uses the `keys()` method to get an array of keys (dates) from the grouped collection, and finally converts this collection into a plain PHP array using `all()`. The result will be an array containing only the dates as you desired:

```php
array:14 [▼ 
 "2024-01-01" 
 "2024-01-02" 
 "2024-01-03" 
 "2024-01-04" 
 "2024-01-05" 
]
```

