To address the `ReferenceError: window is not defined` issue in your Angular 17 SSR application with ApexCharts, you can use the `afterNextRender()` lifecycle hook to ensure that ApexCharts initialization runs only on the client side. Here’s how you can implement it:

```typescript
import { Component, ElementRef, OnInit, ViewChild, afterNextRender } from '@angular/core';
import ApexCharts from 'apexcharts';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-dashboard',
  templateUrl: './dashboard.component.html'
})
export class DashboardComponent implements OnInit {
  @ViewChild('chart') chart!: ElementRef;

  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.chartOptions = {
      series: [
        { name: 'STOCK ABC', data: [/* your data */] }
      ],
      // other chart options
    };
  }

  afterNextRender() {
    const element = this.chart.nativeElement;
    new ApexCharts(element, this.chartOptions).render();
  }
}
```

Ensure `afterNextRender` is called in the component's constructor or a suitable lifecycle hook. This approach leverages `afterNextRender`, which runs only on the client side, preventing the `window` reference error during SSR.

Remember to remove any direct ApexCharts initialization from the `ngOnInit` method to avoid running it server-side.

