```angular-html
<ul>
  @for (item of arr.slice(1); track item) {
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
  }
</ul>
```

In this example, `arr.slice(1)` creates a new array starting from index 1, and the `@for` loop iterates over it. The `track item` ensures Angular can efficiently manage DOM updates.

This approach leverages the `slice` method to exclude the first element before rendering the remaining items in the list.

