The issue you're encountering likely stems from the fact that the `deleted_at` column was not properly added to your database table during migration. Ensure you have correctly applied the `softDeletes()` method in your migration file:

```php
Schema::table('users', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->softDeletes();
});
```

After making this change, run a fresh migration to apply the schema changes:

```bash
php artisan migrate:fresh
```

This command will drop and recreate all tables, ensuring that the `deleted_at` column is properly added. If you only need to add the column without dropping existing data, use:

```bash
php artisan migrate:refresh
```

Additionally, verify your model uses the `SoftDeletes` trait correctly:

```php
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\SoftDeletes;

class User extends Authenticatable
{
    use SoftDeletes;
}
```

