```angular-html
@for (user of users; track user.id; let i = $index) {
  {{ user.name + i }}
}
@empty {
  Empty list of users 
}
```

This syntax correctly defines `i` as the index variable, allowing you to use it in your template. Note that `$index` is always available within `@for` blocks and can be aliased for clarity or specific needs.

