In Laravel 11, you can instruct Laravel to auto-discover event listeners from a custom directory by modifying your `bootstrap/app.php` file. Specifically, you need to use the `withEvents` method within the `$app->configureEventDiscovery()` call. Here’s how:

```php
$app->configureEventDiscovery(function ($events) {
    $events->discover(__DIR__.'/../app/Domain/Listeners');
});
```

This code tells Laravel to scan the specified directory for event listeners. If you have multiple directories, you can add them as an array:

```php
$app->configureEventDiscovery(function ($events) {
    $events->discover([
        __DIR__.'/../app/Domain/Listeners',
        __DIR__.'/../path/to/another/listener/directory',
    ]);
});
```

After making this change, Laravel will automatically discover and register event listeners from the specified directories. You can verify the registered listeners using the `event:list` Artisan command:

```shell
php artisan event:list
```

This approach leverages Laravel’s auto-discovery feature to keep your code organized in custom directories while maintaining ease of use.

