The error `NG05105` suggests that there's an unexpected synthetic listener attached to your `@transformPanel.done`. This typically happens when you're using Angular Material components without the necessary animations module imported.

Ensure you import `BrowserAnimationsModule` in your root `AppModule`, as it is required for Angular Material components. Here’s how you can do it:

```typescript
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';
// Other imports...

@NgModule({
  declarations: [AppComponent],
  imports: [
    BrowserModule,
    // Other modules...
  ],
  providers: [],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule { }
```

If `BrowserAnimationsModule` is already imported, try importing `NoopAnimationsModule` instead. This can be useful in development environments where you want to disable animations for performance reasons:

```typescript
import { NoopAnimationsModule } from '@angular/platform-browser/animations';

@NgModule({
  // Other configurations...
  imports: [
    NoopAnimationsModule,
    // Other modules...
  ]
})
export class AppModule { }
```

Make sure all your components are correctly declared and imported, especially those using Angular Material directives. Your current setup looks mostly correct, but ensure that `FormsModule` is also included if you're using any form-related features.

Restarting the server after making these changes might resolve the issue.

