To customize the icons for the service section in Klaro (like using "+" and "-" for open/close states), you can leverage CSS transitions along with custom HTML elements within your Klaro configuration. However, Klaro itself does not provide direct options to change these icons out of the box.

You can achieve this by:

1. **Customizing the Template**: Modify the template used by Klaro to include your custom icons.
2. **Using CSS Transitions**: Apply transitions for smooth icon changes as the service section opens and closes.

Here’s a brief example:

```html
<!-- Custom template in klaro configuration -->
<klaro [config]="{
  // other configurations...
  cookie: {
    name: 'yourCookieName',
    path: '/',
    expires: 365,
    domain: '.yourdomain.com'
  },
  service: {
    title: 'Services',
    items: [
      { id: 'service1', label: 'Service 1' },
      // other services...
    ],
    template: `
      <div class="klaro-service">
        <span>{{ item.label }}</span>
        <button (click)="toggle(item)">
          <i [ngClass]="{ 'fa-plus': !item.open, 'fa-minus': item.open }"></i>
        </button>
      </div>
    `
  }
}"
></klaro>
```

In your component:

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-your-component',
  templateUrl: './your-component.component.html'
})
export class YourComponent {
  toggle(item) {
    item.open = !item.open;
  }
}
```

And add the necessary Font Awesome imports or equivalent for icon classes.

This approach allows you to customize the icons and control their display based on the service section's open/closed state.

