The issue arises from how you're managing the `selectedButtons` state and its interaction with checkboxes. Ensure each checkbox updates the corresponding button's selection individually. Here’s a revised approach:

1. **Update Checkbox Handling**: Each checkbox should update only its respective button in `selectedButtons`.

2. **Form Update**: Ensure form submission correctly captures these selections.

Here is an updated snippet for your Vue component:

```vue
<template>
  <!-- Buttons Section -->
  <div v-for="button in buttons" :key="button.id">
    <input 
      type="checkbox"
      :value="button.buttonTitle"
      @change="updateSelectedButtons(button.buttonTitle)"
      v-model="selectedButtons"
    />
    {{ button.buttonTitle }}
  </div>

  <!-- Form Submit -->
  <form @submit.prevent="submitForm">
    <!-- Other form fields... -->
    <input type="hidden" :value="selectedButtons" name="buttons" />
    <button type="submit">Send Message</button>
  </form>
</template>

<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue';
import { useForm } from '@inertiajs/vue3';

const selectedButtons = ref([]);

// Update the selected buttons when a checkbox changes
function updateSelectedButtons(buttonTitle) {
  if (selectedButtons.value.includes(buttonTitle)) {
    selectedButtons.value = selectedButtons.value.filter(b => b !== buttonTitle);
  } else {
    selectedButtons.value.push(buttonTitle);
  }
}

const form = useForm({
  title: null,
  body: null,
  chatID: [],
  channelID: [],
  buttons: selectedButtons.value, // Initialize with selected buttons
  images: [],
  date: null,
  time: null,
});

function submitForm() {
  form.post('/message');
}
</script>
```

This ensures that only the selected checkboxes are included in `selectedButtons`, and these selections are correctly sent to your backend.

