The issue arises because `$homeInfo` might be `null`, and you're trying to access properties on a null object. To avoid this, ensure that `$homeInfo` is not null before accessing its properties. You can use the null coalescing operator (`??`) or check if it's not null.

Here’s how you can modify your Blade template:

```blade
@php
    $heroImage = $homeInfo?->where('pag_name', 'hero_image')->first();
@endphp

@if ($heroImage)
    {{ $heroImage->pag_value }}
@endif
```

This checks if `$homeInfo` is not null before calling `where`, ensuring that you don't encounter the "Attempt to read property on null" error.

Alternatively, you can directly check and display:

```blade
@php
    $heroImage = $homeInfo?->where('pag_name', 'hero_image')->first();
@endphp

{{ optional($homeInfo)->where('pag_name', 'hero_image')->first()->pag_value ?? '' }}
```

Using `optional` from the Illuminate\Support\Facades package, you can safely access properties without worrying about null values.

This approach ensures that your code handles cases where `$homeInfo` might be null gracefully.

