To enable file downloads from both views, you can create a `download` method in your `UploadController`. This method will handle downloading the file based on the upload ID passed via route parameters.

First, define the route for the download action:

```php
Route::get('/uploads/{upload}/download', [App\Http\Controllers\UploadController::class, 'download'])->name('uploads.download');
```

Next, implement the `download` method in your `UploadController`:

```php
public function download(Upload $upload)
{
    return response()->download(storage_path('app/public/' . $upload->path));
}
```

In both views (`index` and `show`), add links to trigger the download. For example, in the `index` view:

```blade
@foreach ($uploads as $upload)
    <a href="{{ route('uploads.download', ['upload' => $upload]) }}">Download {{ $upload->name }}</a>
@endforeach
```

And in the `show` view:

```blade
<a href="{{ route('uploads.download', ['upload' => $upload]) }}">Download</a>
```

This setup ensures that clicking on a link will trigger a file download from either view, making your implementation both clean and efficient.

