The issue lies in how you're loading the related `typeEducation` data for the single education record in your `edit` method of `EducationController`. You are using `$education->load(['typeEducation']);`, but this should be `with('typeEducation')` when returning the resource. Here's the corrected code:

```php
public function edit(Education $education): Response
{
    return Inertia::render('School/Education/Edit', [
        'education' => new EducationResource($education->load(['typeEducation'])),
        'educationTypes' => EducationTypeResource::collection(EducationType::all())
    ]);
}
```

Ensure that the `EducationResource` class correctly handles null values for related data. You can modify your resource to return null if the relationship is not loaded:

```php
class EducationResource extends JsonResource
{
    public function toArray(Request $request): array
    {
        return [
            'id' => $this->id,
            'title' => $this->whenLoaded('typeEducation', fn () => $this->typeEducation?->title),
            'isActive' => $this->is_active,
            'startDate' => $this->start_date,
            'endDate' => $this->end_date,
            'educationTypes' => EducationTypeResource::collection($this->whenLoaded('educationTypes'))
        ];
    }
}
```

This ensures that `typeEducation->title` returns null if the relationship is not loaded, preventing the "Attempt to read property on null" error.

