The issue arises because `MenuItemComponent` expects an input of type `MenuItem | undefined`, but in your template, you're using a simple string variable named `item`. To resolve this, ensure that the `item` used in the template matches the expected type. Since `menu` is defined as an array of `MenuItem` objects, use the correct type when binding to `item`.

In your `app.component.html`, change:

```html
@for (item of menu; track item.id) {
```

To:

```html
@for (item of menu; track item.id) {
  <menu-item [item]="item"></menu-item>
}
```

This binds each `MenuItem` from the `menu` array to the `item` input in `MenuItemComponent`, ensuring type compatibility. Make sure that `MenuItem` is correctly defined as:

```typescript
export type MenuItem = {
  id: number,
  category: ItemCategory,
  sub_category?: string,
  name: string,
  price: number
}
```

This change ensures the types are aligned, resolving the compilation error.

