The error message `NG5002: Cannot parse expression. @for loop expression must match the pattern " of "` suggests a syntax issue in your template's `@for` directive usage. Ensure that your `@for` loop follows the correct format, which includes specifying the collection and the track expression.

For example:

```angular-html
@Component({
  template: `
    <ul>
      @for (item of items; track item.id) {
        <li>{{ item.name }}</li>
      }
    </ul>
  `,
})
class MyComponent {
  items = [
    { id: 1, name: 'Item 1' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Item 2' },
  ];
}
```

Here, `track item.id` ensures that each item is uniquely identified. If you encounter this error, check your template for any syntax mistakes or missing parts in the `@for` loop pattern.

For more detailed guidance and examples, refer to the Angular documentation on [ngForOf](https://angular.io/api/common/NgForOf).

