To address the issue of displaying a loading status during lazy-loaded route transitions in your Angular application, you can use a global loading indicator. Here’s how:

1. **Create a Loading Component**: First, create a simple `LoadingComponent` that will display a spinner or any other loading message.

2. **Update Routing Configuration**: Modify the routing configuration to include a default path for showing the loading component when lazy-loaded modules are being loaded.

Here's an example of how you can implement this:

1. **Create Loading Component**:
   ```typescript
   // src/app/loading/loading.component.ts
   import { Component } from '@angular/core';

   @Component({
     selector: 'app-loading',
     template: `<div>Loading...</div>`
   })
   export class LoadingComponent {}
   ```

2. **Update `app-routing.module.ts`**:
   ```typescript
   // src/app/app-routing.module.ts
   import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
   import { RouterModule, Routes } from '@angular/router';

   const routes: Routes = [
     {
       path: '',
       redirectTo: '/dashboard',
       pathMatch: 'full'
     },
     {
       path: 'login',
       component: LoginComponent,
       title: 'Login'
     },
     {
       path: '',
       canActivateChild: [AuthGuard],
       loadChildren: () => import(`./app-authorized.routes`).then((r) => r.appAuthorizedRoutes),
       // Add a default route for loading
       children: [
         { path: '', component: LoadingComponent }
       ]
     },
     { path: '**', redirectTo: '/dashboard' }
   ];

   @NgModule({
     imports: [RouterModule.forRoot(routes)],
     exports: [RouterModule]
   })
   export class AppRoutingModule {}
   ```

3. **Update `app.component.html`**:
   ```html
   <!-- src/app/app.component.html -->
   <router-outlet></router-outlet>
   ```

With these changes, when the user logs in and is redirected to a lazy-loaded route, the application will display the loading component until the module is fully loaded. This improves the user experience by providing feedback during the transition period.

