To set up locale-based routing in your Laravel Inertia application, you can use URL defaults as shown below:

1. Define a middleware for setting the locale based on the URL parameter:
```php
class SetLocaleMiddleware {
    public function handle($request, Closure $next) {
        if ($locale = $request->route('locale')) {
            App::setLocale($locale);
        }
        return $next($request);
    }
}
```

2. Register this middleware in `app/Http/Kernel.php`:
```php
protected $middlewareAliases = [
    'setLocale' => \App\Http\Middleware\SetLocaleMiddleware::class,
];
```

3. Use URL defaults to set the default locale for URLs:
```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\URL;

public function boot()
{
    URL::defaults(['locale' => 'en']);
}
```

4. Update your `web.php` routes:
```php
Route::middleware(['setLocale'])->prefix('{locale?}')->group(function () {
    Route::resource('posts', PostController::class);
    Route::resource('comments', CommentController::class);
});
```

This setup ensures that the locale is set based on the URL parameter, with 'en' as the default. The `SetLocaleMiddleware` logs the correct locale from the URL, and Inertia should correctly pick up the locale for your Vue components using `{{ $t('text') }}`.

