To display items from index 1 of an array of strings in Angular, you can use the `@for` block with a track expression and leverage the `$index` variable to skip the first item. Here's how:

```angular-html
<ul>
  @for (item of arr; track $index) {
    {{ item }}
  }
</ul>
```

However, since we want to start from index 1, you can use a conditional check inside the loop or filter the array before rendering it. A cleaner approach is to filter the array in your component:

```typescript
// ingredient-list.component.ts
@Component({
  selector: 'app-ingredient-list',
  template: `
    <ul>
      @for (item of arr.slice(1); track $index) {
        {{ item }}
      }
    </ul>
  `,
})
export class IngredientListComponent {
  arr = ["str1", "str2", "str3", "str4", "str5"];
}
```

This solution uses `slice(1)` to exclude the first element before rendering with `@for`.

