The issue likely stems from the fact that `charts` is not marked as an `OnPush` component dependency. When `typeSignal()` changes, Angular does not automatically detect this change because `charts` is computed but not properly tracked by the component's change detection mechanism.

To resolve this, ensure your `charts` signal is correctly set up to be reactive and track dependencies:

1. Mark `charts` as a dependency of `typeSignal`.
2. Use `computed` with proper tracking in your component class.

Here’s how you can adjust your code:

```typescript
import { computed } from '@angular/core';

// Ensure typeSignal is an input signal
this.typeSignal = input.required<string>();

// Define charts as a computed signal that depends on typeSignal
charts = computed(() => {
  const chartsArr: ChartData[] = [];
  if (this.typeSignal() === "OIA") {
    // ... your logic ...
  } else if (this.typeSignal() === "Portail de l'information") {
    // ... your logic ...
  } else if (this.typeSignal() === "Bulletin Board") {
    // ... your logic ...
  }
  console.log(chartsArr);
  return structuredClone(chartsArr);
}, [this.typeSignal()]);
```

By adding `[this.typeSignal()]` as a dependency, you ensure that `charts` updates whenever `typeSignal` changes. This should make the charts update correctly in your template when the radio buttons are toggled.

