In Angular 17, you can use the `$index` variable within `@for` blocks instead of the `index` keyword used in `*ngFor`. The `$index` variable represents the zero-based index of the current item in the iteration. Here’s how you can define and use it:

```angular-html
@for (user of users; track user.id; let i = $index) {
  {{ user.name + i }}
}
@empty {
  Empty list of users 
}
```

This code snippet correctly uses `$index` to get the index of each `user` in the iteration. Note that you don't need to add a semicolon after `track user.id`; it should be directly followed by `let i = $index`.

