The issue you're encountering stems from how data is passed to anonymous components in Blade templates. When using `@props` or `x-data` (in Livewire) with anonymous components, the variables must be explicitly passed via attributes starting with a colon (`:`).

In your case, since `user_preference.blade.php` contains conditional logic and you want to pass `$sizes` to an anonymous component called `with_sizes_section`, ensure that `$sizes` is correctly passed as an attribute. Here’s how you can do it:

```blade
@if ($counter > 0)
    <x-with-sizes-section :sizes="{{ $sizes }}" />
@else
    <!-- Other content -->
@endif
```

In the anonymous component `with_sizes_section.blade.php`, you would use the `@props` directive to define which attributes should be considered data variables:

```blade
<!-- /resources/views/components/with_sizes_section.blade.php -->

@props(['sizes'])

<div>
    @foreach ($sizes as $size)
        {{ $size }}
    @endforeach
</div>
```

This setup ensures that `$sizes` is correctly passed and accessible within the anonymous component. Remember, when using `@props`, all other attributes will be available via the attribute bag unless explicitly defined in `@props`.

